  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The strongest signal so far is that multiprofile RNA with avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) substantially outperforms singleprofile RNA (config_001, acc=0.485), and multimodal singleprofile with concat (config_016, acc=0.527) modestly beats rna_only singleprofile. The critical untested question is whether combining the multiprofile advantage with multimodal fusion (keeping the same concat strategy from config_016) can push accuracy beyond the current best of 0.591. config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the minimal, logical extension: it adds multiprofile to the already-tested multimodal+concat setup, isolating the effect of profile setting within the multimodal regime. This is the best use of experiment 5 because it directly tests the most promising unexplored combination; if it exceeds 0.591, we have a new best and can refine fusion/aggregation in remaining experiments, and if it does not, we gain strong evidence to focus remaining budget on rna_only multiprofile variants (e.g., transformer aggregation or alternative encoders)."
}

